;; kaiyaku 解約 — REPRESENTATIVE real-service cancellation-procedure catalog (ADR-2606112201 R1).
;;
;; The R1 data leg: the R0 縁-ledger seed is 9 SYNTHETIC ties; this is the first catalog of
;; REAL services and their disclosed 解約/退会 procedures, so a plan can carry the actual
;; self-submit steps + cost-of-severance (notice / 違約金) instead of a placeholder.
;;
;; HONESTY GATES (read before editing — these are enforced by methods/catalog.cljc + tests):
;;   - :proc/operator-verified is FALSE for every entry. These are :representative disclosed
;;     SHAPES, NOT a live ToS assertion. A vendor changes its procedure at any time; an
;;     operator MUST verify the procedure (and the :proc/cancel stance) against the disclosed
;;     source before ANY live use (G6). karakuri's registry carries the same caveat.
;;   - G3: a :browser stance of :prohibited / :unknown can NEVER derive tier T2 (catalog
;;     derive-tier mirrors plan/select-tier exactly). Major consumer SaaS forbid browser
;;     automation in ToS → they fall to T1 (if a cancel API exists) or T3 self-submit.
;;   - G3: :proc/self-submit-steps are the DISCLOSED official procedure only — no
;;     detection-evasion verb (captcha-solve / proxy-rotate / stealth / …) may appear
;;     (catalog/validate raises; tests enforce).
;;   - G8: :proc/notice-days / :proc/penalty-jpy are the disclosed cost-of-severance, carried
;;     into the plan and NEVER planned around. Where plan-dependent (e.g. Adobe annual ETF),
;;     the value is :representative and the operator must confirm the member's actual plan.
;;   - N1: every entry is a SERVICE, never a person.
;;
;; :proc/cancel sub-keys mirror the ledger's :svc/cancel ({:api :browser :self-submit}) and
;; karakuri's two stance axes (a cancel API can exist while browser automation is forbidden).
